🔢 Dry Run (Very Important)

Initial:

fuel = 10
Iteration 1

Reach station at 10 → push 60

Heap = [60]

Pop 60 → fuel = 70
Stops = 1

Iteration 2

Now fuel = 70

Push stations:
20 → 30
30 → 30
60 → 40

Heap = [40, 30, 30]

Pop 40 → fuel = 110
Stops = 2

Now 110 >= 100

Answer = 2

⏱ Time Complexity

Each station pushed once

Each station popped at most once

Time Complexity =
O(n log n)

📦 Space Complexity

Heap stores at most n stations

O(n)

🧠 Why Greedy Works?

We delay refueling until necessary.

Instead of stopping at every station,
we collect options and pick the best one when needed.

This ensures:
✔ minimum stops
✔ maximum reach
✔ optimal decision

🎯 Edge Cases

If startFuel >= target → return 0

If first station unreachable → return -1

If no stations → return -1 unless startFuel >= target

💬 Interview Answer Summary (Short Version)

Use a greedy strategy with max-heap. Add all reachable stations into heap. If stuck, refuel from station with maximum fuel. This ensures minimum stops. Time complexity O(n log n).
